# warnings

## UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import defer` is currently lowered to a normal import, because the build has a static import cycle. This changes execution timing because side effects run immediately instead of when the deferred import is first used. `experimental.importDefer` does not keep the deferred evaluation in this build yet.
   ╭─[ main.js:2:1 ]
   │
 2 │ import defer * as ns from './a.js';
   │ ─────────────────┬─────────────────  
   │                  ╰─────────────────── The deferred phase is removed here.
───╯

```

# Assets

## main.js

```js
// c.js
globalThis.order.push("c sees " + typeof bar);
function baz() {
	return "baz";
}
// a.js
globalThis.order.push("a sees " + typeof baz);
const foo = String("foo");
// y.js
globalThis.order.push("y");
// b.js
globalThis.order.push("b sees " + foo);
function bar() {
	return "bar";
}
// z.js
globalThis.order.push("z");
// main.js
const access = () => foo;
export { access };

```
